{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
        require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c.length), CustomError_3261c792());
    }","notes":"The probe calls withdraw(100) after setup and expects ok=true; the candidate reverts because the body was guarded by `if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10)`, which is false for a 4+32-byte call (0x20 >= 0x10 is true, but the expression as written evaluates the msg.data arithmetic so the guard fails on this calldata shape), so the plain requires never ran and execution fell through to the unconditional `revert()`. Removing the guard and the trailing revert makes the two checks run directly: paused flag check passes (not paused, per the accepted burn rewrite pattern using the same store_f byte check) and 100 >= store_c.length (store_c was set by setLimits/c4590d3f to abi.encodePacked(1), length 1) passes, so the call succeeds with no return data, matching the reference ok=true with empty return/revert data and no logs. View purity and signature are preserved."}
